Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: clear hardware frame accounting on reset

The XR500v station hardware cap counts frames awaiting a TX status or
power-save loopback. A watchdog reset discards hardware queues and RX
rings, so those notifications may never arrive. The surviving stations
keep stale hw_pending counts and can remain on TX_HOLD until the fallback
resynchronization releases them.

Clear each station's pending count after the reset has discarded TX and
RX rings, before restarting DMA. Release its hold through the existing
helper so its TX queues are scheduled again. The TX worker, RX/TX NAPI
and pre-TBTT tasklet are still disabled at this point.

Keep host power-save queues intact. Their frames have already left the
hardware and are counted again when submitted, independently of the old
hardware debt. Non-station WCIDs are skipped.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/mt7603/mac.c b/mt7603/mac.c
--- a/mt7603/mac.c
+++ b/mt7603/mac.c
@@ -1444,6 +1444,26 @@
 	mt76_clear(dev, MT_SCH_4, MT_SCH_4_RESET);
 }
 
+static void mt7603_hw_pending_reset(struct mt7603_dev *dev)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	for (i = 0; i < MT7603_WTBL_STA; i++) {
+		struct mt76_wcid *wcid = mt76_wcid_ptr(dev, i);
+		struct mt7603_sta *msta;
+
+		if (!wcid || !wcid->sta)
+			continue;
+
+		msta = container_of(wcid, struct mt7603_sta, wcid);
+		atomic_set(&msta->hw_pending, 0);
+		WRITE_ONCE(msta->hw_settled, jiffies);
+		mt7603_hw_release(dev, msta);
+	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+}
+
 static void mt7603_mac_watchdog_reset(struct mt7603_dev *dev)
 {
 	int beacon_int = dev->mt76.beacon_int;
@@ -1494,6 +1514,9 @@
 	    (dev->cur_reset_cause == RESET_CAUSE_BEACON_STUCK &&
 	     dev->reset_cause[RESET_CAUSE_BEACON_STUCK] >= 2))
 		mt7603_pse_reset(dev);
+
+	/* TX and RX rings are discarded before the accounting is reset. */
+	mt7603_hw_pending_reset(dev);
 
 	if (!dev->reset_cause[RESET_CAUSE_RESET_FAILED]) {
 		mt7603_mac_dma_start(dev);
